== P-7, THE EXECUTE HALF, against live project uccixoonmbhrnyczyigt
== 23 September 2026, rolled back

Run through `mcp__Supabase__apply_migration`. Verbatim:

  ERROR:  P0001: PROBE ALL PASS (rolled back). 22 refusals over 11 verbs and
  2 roles, 0 reached a body. THE CONTROL ANSWERED: escrow_admin_resolve, under
  role authenticated in the same transaction, returned {"status": "forbidden"}.
  This is the EXECUTE layer; the HTTP layer is a separate claim and is not made
  here.

ELEVEN VERBS, TWO ROLES, TWENTY TWO REFUSALS. Every one raised
`insufficient_privilege` (42501) before its body ran. The eleven are the four
F-2 revoked, their `_as` siblings, the service path `escrow_hold`, the two new
proposal doors from 23 September, the generic `escrow_open`, and the evidence
door.

THE CONTROL IS THE LINE THAT MAKES THE OTHER TWENTY TWO MEAN ANYTHING.
`escrow_admin_resolve` is granted to `authenticated` deliberately, and under
the identical role switch, in the same transaction, it returned
`{"status": "forbidden"}`. That is a business answer in escrow's own
vocabulary. So the harness reaches function bodies, and a refusal above is a
refusal rather than a broken call.

WHAT THIS DOES NOT PROVE, STATED PLAINLY. It does not prove the HTTP half.
PostgREST resolves a call by argument NAME and serves from a schema cache, so
a door can be shut in `pg_proc` and still answerable over the wire by an
overload or a stale cache entry. That is `escrow_revoke.sh` and it has not
run: see escrow_revoke.log for the egress denial, re-checked today.

P-7 IS THEREFORE NOT CLOSED. It is half proved, and the half that is proved is
named rather than counted as the whole.

